{"title":"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(intuitive,_fun)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (intuitive, fun)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Chubby makes nonstandard checkerboards that have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squares on each side.  The checkerboards have a black square in every corner and alternate red and black squares along every row and column.  How many black squares are there on such a checkerboard?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3321bd867435343d4609d5a67f31582051a5ae5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 480 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 481 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 482 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 483 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 484$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"440\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 15 rows with 15 black tiles, and 16 rows with 16 black tiles, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a7ec21efc5a28ea5a4b918600cebd8ce61d6d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^2+16^2 =225+256= \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 481}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"271\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Note: When solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bade9c1fe9e69f976dbef4cf4458c5671671ecf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />+<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/5962bd17aa962087061b2201d2e0a8026ebd5cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, you only need to calculate the units digit.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We build the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548e2efae35789acbb32e297acc17e7ac0ad947e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\times 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> checkerboard starting with a board of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ac5f036c91d2384577c1ac04612b08abb481b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\times 30$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> that is exactly half black.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91bc020f9815a9a48e144ddb4ef48d5e43297d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> black tiles in this region.\n</p><p>Add to this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ac5f036c91d2384577c1ac04612b08abb481b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\times 30$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> checkerboard a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b537396c15430d63cb19fb5bc349a96e713d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> strip on the bottom that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> black tiles.\n</p><p>Add to this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c4786c7ab2977f8c82ef4caf5cbef0b5ad5d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\times 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> checkerboard a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d801e0cfb00b1167f34ef43b7131cd88d29ac520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> strip on the right that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e4fe246e6c6322be6dde23ca8a681339088223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> black tiles.\n</p><p>In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfef1fd5f5ba00828728e40d3657beadad0c560b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 30 + 15 + 15 + 1 = 481$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"212\" height=\"14\" /> tiles, giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94ebbcee4425943359f924c2b7a67f7dfdaa8cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 481}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/4272db7fd3b90867ad13324fcb38f8ef0dd3a838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> strip, there are 31 black tiles and 31 white tiles. There are 15 such strips in total and another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13dea87b9abdd4f769fcc317d5b3074a9e25f512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> strip having 16 black titles.\n</p><p>In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d6427619cb0048f98131bc902d42aab0dd9dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31\\times 15+16=481$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"15\" /> black tiles.\n</p><p>~Bran_Quin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drawing smaller scale sketches, we notice that the odd columns of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd) board have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711fb96d5f47414b7f68114c27aa58e388ead3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lceil \\frac{n}{2} \\right \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"30\" height=\"33\" /> black tiles, while the even columns have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529ed29729a2b2403d8c85740261c03bbc9ccb6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"30\" height=\"33\" /> black tiles. In our case, we have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548e2efae35789acbb32e297acc17e7ac0ad947e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 \\times 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> board. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> odd columns, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> even columns, so the number of black tiles in total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14bb36fe075745656da53cdcd00981af10b5458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16^2 + 15^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 481}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"172\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~kn07\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28intuitive.2C_fun.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(intuitive,_fun)\">Solution 5 (intuitive, fun)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (intuitive, fun)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a “snake” that begins at the leftmost vertex and travels down and up. In the first column, there are 16 black squares, and in the second, there are 15. This process repeats for the remaining rows, until the last, in which we end with 16. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b80af936d102e5ae58859f28c675dd571047002.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16^2 + 15^2 = \\boxed{481}\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f669669e3e9848f2b03c6b15cb55fc2a258fcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> squares on the board; we can relate this board to an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d8c0ffa3981f1a8bb1f59888a104d31818ce12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 * 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> board and find a nice trick. In an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d8c0ffa3981f1a8bb1f59888a104d31818ce12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 * 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> board, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae92a1d95a7555e7f10eb53ba4ada5bbb28c384.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> squares and an even number of red and black squares. When we convert this grid into a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16bf09a34a50248bca404509b854f70879f0482d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 by 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> grid, we add an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />- shape along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edges of the square that contributes a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04f057692c195debe57fe7caea1c4ebdba0ec15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9*2 -1=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" /> new squares. Now we must fix the bottom new corner either red or black; once we do this, we also fix the top right and bottom left squares, which forces there to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of one color and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of another. This will cause the whole grid to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> of one color and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of another.\n</p><p>We can apply the same logic to this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/51222b0866b1ccf5cc221c5bd21f9600e59a2e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 *31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> grid by relating it to a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd75232621125889242d5efd6f044966b89b2a55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 * 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> grid with an even number of red and black squares. We add an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> Shape of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edaeba3a47089bd67be01d3263b5b12615738a59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31* -1=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. And of these new squares, the bottom corner, the top right, and the bottom left will all be black. Causing there to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> new black squares and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> new red squares. This means the total number of black squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315b0b4922f3060ca9ba322e4cc2de587c962b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30^2}{2} +31=\\boxed{481}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-